				<guid>http://localhost:1313/posts/migration-from-wix-to-github-pages-and-hugo/</guid>
				<description>&lt;p&gt;&lt;em&gt;My journey of migrating dynamicallyblunttech.com using Hugo, Markdown, Congo and GitHub Actions — including custom Python scripts, media extraction, a few surprises, and the things I am still figuring out.&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;There is something interesting about being a backend developer.&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;You spend most of your working hours building systems, designing APIs, debugging production issues and figuring out why something that worked yesterday suddenly doesn&amp;rsquo;t work today.&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;Then one day, you decide to build your &lt;strong&gt;personal blog&lt;/strong&gt;.&lt;/p&gt;</description>
