			<item>
				<title>Dynamic Scheduling any REST API&#39;s</title>
				<link>http://localhost:1313/posts/dynamic-scheduling-any-rest-api-s/</link>
				<pubDate>Tue, 27 Oct 2026 08:14:31 +0530</pubDate>
				<guid>http://localhost:1313/posts/dynamic-scheduling-any-rest-api-s/</guid>
				<description>&lt;p&gt;Spring boot provides an easy option of scheduling tasks which will be triggered when the interval or time is right. We can use the @Scheduled annotation to achieve this, but what if we want to schedule the jobs on certain events, or by invoking some services.&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;Lets say you are working on a project in which you want to schedule your API&amp;rsquo;s to run at 12:00pm every night and collect the data for the entire day and save it to either in database or in some files. There could be multiple task for which you will invoke other API&amp;rsquo;s such as data collection for specific scenarios, or sending notification or updating the status of certain entity when certain event happened etc.&lt;/p&gt;</description>
			</item>
